  "worked_solution": "When a particle (or object) moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector at time $t$ is given by the equation\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position vector.\n\nIn this case, the skier starts at the origin, so\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=6i-1j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the skier after $t=5\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(0i+0j)+(6i-1j)(5) \\\\  & =(\\,30\\,i-5\\,j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
